<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Max Planck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1858">1858</a>–<a href="/years/1947">1947</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Max Karl Ernst Ludwig Planck</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Max Karl Ernst Ludwig Planck was a German theoretical physicist, the originator of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quantum-mechanics">quantum theory</a> and one of the founders of modern physics. Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiel">Kiel</a>, he studied in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hermann-von-helmholtz">Hermann von Helmholtz</a> and Gustav Kirchhoff and in 1889 succeeded Kirchhoff at the Friedrich Wilhelm <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humboldt-university-of-berlin">University of Berlin</a>. On 14 December 1900 he presented a derivation resting on the supposition that electromagnetic energy could be emitted only as a multiple of an elementary unit, the origin of the Planck constant, h. He received the 1918 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prize</a> in Physics and was twice President of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaiser">Kaiser</a> Wilhelm Society, renamed the Max Planck Society in 1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/max-planck.jpg" alt="Max Planck" width="330" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hugo Erfurth · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Max_Planck_by_Hugo_Erfurth_1938cr_-_restoration1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Before the German Physical Society in Berlin, <b>Max Planck</b> proposed that energy is emitted in discrete packets, or quanta.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-14">14 December in history</a></li></ul></section>
